dm-crypt: read the status after the last reference

Mainline 148845aa1921 ("dm-crypt: fix a tiny race condition in
crypt_dec_pending"), for 7.2, which lacks it. crypt_dec_pending read
io->error before dropping its reference, so an endio that set the
error and dropped its own reference in between was missed: a read
that failed, never decrypted, or a failed write, completed as a
success. It reads the error after atomic_dec_and_test now.

diff --git a/drivers/md/dm-crypt.c b/drivers/md/dm-crypt.c
--- a/drivers/md/dm-crypt.c
+++ b/drivers/md/dm-crypt.c
@@ -1745,7 +1745,6 @@ static void crypt_dec_pending(struct dm_crypt_io *io)
 {
 	struct crypt_config *cc = io->cc;
 	struct bio *base_bio = io->base_bio;
-	blk_status_t error = io->error;
 
 	if (!atomic_dec_and_test(&io->io_pending))
 		return;
@@ -1767,7 +1766,7 @@ static void crypt_dec_pending(struct dm_crypt_io *io)
 	else
 		kfree(io->integrity_metadata);
 
-	base_bio->bi_status = error;
+	base_bio->bi_status = io->error;
 
 	bio_endio(base_bio);
 }
